{%- doc -%}
  Renders the <img> element using provided image object

  @param {object} image - image object
  @param {number} [height] - custom image height
  @param {string} [class] - additional classes
  @param {string} [text_fallback] - text to display if image is blank
  @param {boolean} [unset_image_tag] - if true, ignores the image focal point
  @param {string} [style] - additional styles
  @param {string} [alt_text_fallback] - Optional text to display if image alt text is blank
  @param {string} [fetchpriority] - 'high' for the page's LCP image, otherwise omit
  @param {string} [sizes] - responsive sizes attribute; when given, switches to a
    width-based srcset (matching sections/hero.liquid's convention) instead of the
    default 1x/2x/3x pixel-density srcset, so mobile doesn't download a desktop-sized
    image

  @example
  {% render 'image', image: product.featured_image, height: 300, class: 'product-image' %}
{%- enddoc -%}
{% if image != blank %}
  {% if height %}
    {% assign image_height = height %}
  {% else %}
    {% comment %}
      No explicit height given - falls back to the source image's own
      native height. Uncapped, this requested full-resolution originals
      for large uploaded photos regardless of how small they actually
      render (a 6MB+ hero image at native res was the biggest LCP
      bottleneck on the homepage). Capping the fallback keeps every
      existing explicit height: param untouched while preventing any
      no-height caller from ever requesting more than needed.
    {% endcomment %}
    {% assign image_height = image.height | at_most: 1200 %}
  {% endif %}
  {% comment %}
    The 1x fallback above is capped, but multiplying it by 2/3 for the
    retina variants defeated that cap for any source taller than 400/600px -
    a 1200px-capped image still produced a 3600px 3x request whenever the
    native photo was that tall. Shopify's CDN won't upscale past the source
    image's actual resolution, so this only matters when the native photo
    is large enough to honor the bigger request - which most uploaded
    photos are. Capping each variant against both the multiplied value and
    a flat retina-safe ceiling keeps every existing caller's visual quality
    (still up to 3x pixel density) while removing the unbounded case.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign image_height_2x = image_height | times: 2 | at_most: 2000 %}
  {% assign image_height_3x = image_height | times: 3 | at_most: 2400 %}
  {% assign image_alt_text = image.alt | default: alt_text_fallback | default: '' %}

  {% capture image_srcset -%}
    {{ image | image_url: height: image_height, quality: 65, format: 'webp' }} 1x, {{ image | image_url: height: image_height_2x, quality: 65, format: 'webp' }} 2x, {{ image | image_url: height: image_height_3x, quality: 65, format: 'webp' }} 3x
  {%- endcapture %}

  {% assign style_value = style | default: '' %}

  {% if unset_image_tag %}
    {% assign style_value = style_value | append: 'object-position: inherit;' %}
  {% endif %}

  {% assign loading_value = 'lazy' %}
  {% if fetchpriority == 'high' %}
    {% assign loading_value = 'eager' %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if sizes %}
    {{
      image
      | image_url: width: 1600, quality: 65, format: 'webp'
      | image_tag:
        widths: '400, 600, 832, 1200, 1600, 2000, 2560',
        sizes: sizes,
        class: class,
        style: style_value,
        alt: image_alt_text,
        fetchpriority: fetchpriority,
        loading: loading_value
    }}
  {% else %}
    {{
      image
      | image_url: height: image_height, quality: 65, format: 'webp'
      | image_tag: class: class, srcset: image_srcset, style: style_value, alt: image_alt_text, fetchpriority: fetchpriority, loading: loading_value
    }}
  {% endif %}
{% elsif text_fallback %}
  {{ text_fallback }}
{% endif %}
